esidential mortgages, agricultural, consumer, residential real estate mortgage, and agricultural real estate and production loans. In addition, the company offers debit and credit cards; insurance brokerage; trust and wealth management; online banking solutions, such as access to account balances, online transfers, online bill payment, and electronic delivery of customer statements; mobile banking solutions comprising remote check deposits with mobile bill pay; night depository; direct deposit; cashier's and travelers checks; letters of credit; and ITMs and ATMs. Further, it provides cash management deposit products, such as lockbox, remote deposit capture, positive pay, reverse positive pay, account reconciliation services, zero balance accounts, and sweep accounts; and banking services through telephone, mail, and personal appointments. Additionally, the company offers treasury management services, including balance reporting, transfers between accounts, wire transfer initiation, automated clearing house origination, and stop payments. It operates in Arkansas, Kansas, Missouri, and Oklahoma. Equity Bancshares, Inc. was founded in 1985 and is headquartered in Wichita, Kansas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brad S. Elliott | Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 909 people. Revenue per employee of $231K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $42K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Equity Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.0B market cap on $210M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $38M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.26\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 13.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 211% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.1050279716077123},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.3pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why (EQBK) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Why_EQBK_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_111126125001_1794376201.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794376201.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Equity Bancshares (EQBK) Stock May Be Below Fair Value On Earnings Power","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-eqbk/equity-bancshares/news/equity-bancshares-eqbk-stock-may-be-below-fair-value-on-earn","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794309851.712,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.968,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Third Quarter 10 Q Filing Might Change The Case For Investing In Equity Bancshares (EQBK)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-eqbk/equity-bancshares/news/third-quarter-10-q-filing-might-change-the-case-for-investin","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794216307.195,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Equity Bancshares (EQBK) Eyes Lincoln 